*&———————————————————————*

- 1. ZTB_A2R_CONFTAB1.PSPNR stores INTERNAL number, not external PSPID
- - Must query PROJS/PROJ to convert PSPNR → PSPID
- 
- 1. IMPR.POSNR is already zero-padded (00000011 format)
- - Use ALPHA conversion for consistency with manual entry
- 
- 1. Use PROJS table for template queries (standard WBS structure)
- - Fallback to PROJ if needed
- 
- 1. Use PRPSS table for WBS element hierarchy
- - PSPHI field contains parent internal number
- 
- 1. POSID vs PSPID formats:
- - POSID: PC.000001 (WBS element external ID)
- - PSPID: PC.000001.00.0.0.0 (full project/WBS external ID)
- - PSPNR: 00000077 (internal number for both)
- 
- 1. Field mappings verified from screenshots:
- - PRPSS.PSPNR → ZTB_A2R_WBSITEM.POSNR (internal number)
- - PRPSS.POSID → display ID
- - PRPSS.POST1 → description
- - PRPSS.PSPHI → parent hierarchy
